<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berengar II of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900–966</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Berengar of Ivrea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berengar II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> who seized the Italian crown with his son Adalbert in 950. His imprisonment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-saxe-meiningen">Queen Adelaide</a> brought the German king Otto I into Italy, and in 952 Berengar had to accept Otto as overlord and cede the marches of Verona and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>. Otto deposed him in 961, and he died a prisoner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berengar-ii-of-italy.jpg" alt="Berengar II of Italy" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artwork: Creators of the Chronicle of Bishop Otto of Freising; Photo: AndreasPraefcke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_I_Manuscriptum_Mediolanense_c_1200.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
